# Gate rubric

What the `gate` skill and `evaluator` agent check, before any person reviews work. Sensors (`scripts/harness_check.py`) run first; this rubric is the judgement layer on top. The rubric is rebuilt for every run from the current scope, ux-context, rules and open feedback, so it grows as the project does.

## Every deliverable

| Check | Fail when | Evidence to cite |
|---|---|---|
| Scope fit | It answers a different question than `context/scope.md` | The scope line it drifts from |
| Feedback fit | Open feedback addressed to this deliverable is ignored, or resolved feedback is reopened | Feedback ID |
| Committed decisions | It contradicts a Committed row in `docs/decisions.md` | Decision ID |
| Done-criteria | It misses what was agreed as "done" before the work started | The criterion |

## Research deliverables

| Check | Fail when | Evidence to cite |
|---|---|---|
| Traceability | An insight has no source in `work/research/` | Insight ID |
| Goal fit | It drifts from the research question in the brief | Brief line |
| Constraint distilled | A load-bearing finding is not written into `context/ux-context.md` as a constraint | Insight ID |
| Honest confidence | A claim is stated more strongly than its evidence supports | Claim and source |

## Design deliverables

| Check | Fail when | Evidence to cite |
|---|---|---|
| Mental model first | Screens exist with no agreed model / IA behind them | Missing file |
| Research fit | A design choice contradicts a finding in `context/ux-context.md` | Constraint line |
| Rails | A value or component is not in `system/` | Element and value |
| Component boundaries | A component is used for something its "Must never become" forbids | Component name |
| Heuristics | Clear usability heuristic breach (visibility of status, error prevention, recognition over recall…) | Screen and element |
| Accessibility | Contrast, target size, focus order, labels, motion | Element and measured value |
| States | Missing empty / loading / error / success / edge states | Screen |
| Taste | Generic, default-looking output: it would still work with a competitor's name swapped in | What makes it generic |

Weighting: judge **coherence of the whole flow** and **distinctiveness** at least as hard as craft. Models produce tidy craft by default; what they miss is whether the experience hangs together and belongs to this product.

## Findings format

| Check | Severity (fail/warn) | Evidence | Fix or flag |
|---|---|---|---|

Then one verdict line: `Ready for review` or `N fails: not ready`. The evaluator reports; it does not fix.

